  "limitations": [
    "The real guest checks cover executable VFS ownership, caller credentials, file service/topology and a one-CPU normal-image boot. Native mcexec application execution has not run; procfs/exe publication, PPD/VM/pinning, launch packets and syscall forwarding remain open.",
    "Credential and replacement concurrency use separate four-worker fork phases on each ABI. This is not same-TGID pthread stress. The inherited-descriptor owner-isolation child explicitly closes its executable before exit.",
    "Native process retirement currently follows the final IHK file binding. Complete process-exit cleanup, including abrupt exit while another process keeps an inherited file open, remains part of the pending PPD/process lifecycle integration.",
    "All four first failures are preserved in full: missing error constant during build, rejected fixture symlink before boot, and two runtime captures of the incorrect empty-path errno expectation. Failed records with incomplete input lists are retained as captured; they do not receive current compiler-binding credit.",
    "Declared staging/source graph, lifecycle and unsafe-FFI inventory integration and a fresh full suite remain open. This prototype is bound to the exact retained Kbuild sources and guest probes; it does not promote a production gate.",
    "No new project C production bridge was added. Existing compatibility Rust/C consumers, guest image sources and launcher remain unchanged.",
    "Multi-CPU/multi-OS operation, remaining sysfs faults/races, shutdown, full Rust/assembly completion and independent production acceptance remain required by the original goal."
